  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>fitcnb</keyword>
  <short_description>Fit a naive Bayes classifier.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>mdl = fitcnb(X, Y)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>mdl = fitcnb(X, Y, Name, Value)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>label = predict(mdl, Xnew)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[label, score, cost] = predict(mdl, Xnew)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <description>
    <p><b>fitcnb</b> creates a <b>ClassificationNaiveBayes</b> object from numeric predictors <b>X</b> and class labels <b>Y</b>.</p>
    <p>The current implementation fits normal predictor distributions. Name-value arguments include <b>ClassNames</b>, <b>Prior</b>, <b>DistributionNames</b>, and <b>Weights</b>. Prediction returns posterior class scores.</p>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[X = [0 0; 0 1; 1 0; 5 5; 5 6; 6 5];
Y = [1; 1; 1; 2; 2; 2];
mdl = fitcnb(X, Y);
[label, score] = predict(mdl, [0.2 0.1; 5.2 5.1])]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
